A set of parameters, b, reflects the impact of changes in x on the probability. A suitable model for F(x,b) is assumed, usually considering a normal or logistic distribution. The question of which distribution to use has been widely analyzed, concluding that the two distributions tend to give similar probabilities except in the tails (Ferreira & Couto, 2012; Greene, 2008). According to Greene (2008), in most cases, the choice between these two distributions seems to make little difference. After analyzing both distributions in the present study, the logistic distribution (logit model) was selected because a small improvement in the goodness-of-fit measures was found. Therefore, a logistic distribution was used, giving rise to the following logit model:
