Sónia Soares is a junior research hired under AWAREE project (MIT-EXPL/ STS/0125/2017), which is financed by FCT through national funds, under the MIT Portugal Programme. She has a M. Sc. in Civil Engineering (2018). Her research interests are road safety focusing on driver behavior.
Sara Ferreira is an Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering at University of Porto. She is received his Ph.D. in Transportation Safety from University of Porto in 2010. She has approximately twelve years combined teaching, research and technical experience in transportation safety field, with an extensive published quality papers in peer-review journals or conference proceedings.
António F. Couto is an assistant professor with habilitation at the Faculty of Engineering of the University of Porto (FEUP). He received his PhD from FEUP in 2005. He has been involved in all areas of the transportation planning and engineering sector for more than 30 years and his specialization areas are Transport Economics, Road Safety, Intelligent Transportation Systems and Transportation Planning. He is author of more 80 papers in international journals and conferences. He is also member of several scientific organizations and committees, reviewer of papers to be published in scientific journals and conferences and member of the organizing committee of several international conferences.
